From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
Date: Wed, 28 Oct 2026 17:58:56 +0100
Subject: [PATCH] tapdisk: reduce the timer slack of the IO threads to 5 us

The deferred kick arms deadlines of a few tens of microseconds on the
scheduler of the IO thread of the queue, and select() honours the timer
slack of the thread, 50 us by default: a deadline of 80 us could fire
up to 130 us after it was armed. Set the slack to 5 us in each IO
thread.

The drawback is that the kernel can merge fewer timer expiries, so the
IO threads may wake up a little more often, at a small CPU and power
cost. Only their own timeouts are affected (deferred kick, end of
polling, buffer cache expiry), a handful per queue, and the setting
needs no privilege and doesn't change the scheduling priority.

Assisted-by: Claude Opus 5.5 <noreply@anthropic.com>
Signed-off-by: Emmanuel Varagnat <emmanuel.varagnat@vates.tech>
---
 drivers/tapdisk-server.c | 10 ++++++++++
 1 file changed, 10 insertions(+)

diff --git a/drivers/tapdisk-server.c b/drivers/tapdisk-server.c
index f4f8cdc0..415b0c92 100644
--- a/drivers/tapdisk-server.c
+++ b/drivers/tapdisk-server.c
@@ -30,6 +30,7 @@
 #include <sys/signalfd.h>
 #ifdef HAVE_EVENTFD
 #include <sys/eventfd.h>
+#include <sys/prctl.h>
 #else
 #include <sys/syscall.h>
 #endif
@@ -53,6 +54,13 @@
 #define DBG(_level, _f, _a...)       tlog_write(_level, _f, ##_a)
 #define ERR(_err, _f, _a...)         tlog_error(_err, _f, ##_a)
 
+/*
+ * Timer slack of the IO threads, in nanoseconds. select() may return up to
+ * the slack of the thread after its timeout (50 us by default), too late for
+ * the deferred kick deadline (80 us by default).
+ */
+#define TAPDISK_IO_THREAD_TIMER_SLACK_NS 5000
+
 #define TAPDISK_TIOCBS_PER_QUEUE    (MAX_REQUESTS * BLKIF_MAX_SEGMENTS_PER_REQUEST + 50)
 
 typedef struct tapdisk_server {
@@ -629,6 +637,8 @@ __tapdisk_io_thread_run(void* arg)
 {
 	td_queue_id_t  qid = (unsigned long)arg;
 
+	prctl(PR_SET_TIMERSLACK, TAPDISK_IO_THREAD_TIMER_SLACK_NS);
+
 	while (atomic_load(&server.run))
 		tapdisk_io_iterate(qid);
 
